    "q-334100": {
      "dom_id": "step-q334100",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-x(t)-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-4x(t)-4y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-5,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[1,\\text{ }4]^{T},$ respectively. Which of the following could represent the phase portrait of the system?\n\n*Hint: Here, the dotted line represents the equilibrium solutions.*",
      "worked_solution": "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{-5t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nLet's now sketch the phase portrait.\n\n- First, notice that ${x}_{E}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ are the equilibrium solutions of the system since ${x}_{E}^{′}(t)=0.$ These solutions form the line with the equation $y=-x$ in the phase space, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14255151/assets/29e69d53d09adec27ffc6dee8eb1c343337d0a5c14bedeaaccda5ffb5d6c81bf.png)\n\n- Now, the line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n$y=4x$\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-5t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line. Since ${e}^{-5t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14255151/assets/1babfed2e0d3b7d1c461fb743937afe5d3740b30acae2b165bda1d557d87079b.png)\n\nAll other non-equilibrium solutions are parallel to the vector ${v}_{2}.$ So, the phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14255151/assets/6d78796b92816a9c78ca0f039cbe476116cfc4ba1a0c88380fbbb93fe4b2d49f.png)",
